\title{analyses for Paper III, part II}
\begin{document}

This document builds on ``analyses for Paper III'' (filename ``kuznets.Rnw'') and aims at replicating Björns analyses in stata. Björn has added data to the output of ``kuznets.Rnw'', and saved this in the file ``work1.dta''. The changes include:

\begin{itemize}
\item Adding variables from the VDEM project, specifically data on corruption.
\item LogLog transforming one variable (which one, was it GDP?)
\end{itemize}

Eventually, I would like to be able to replicate Björns data manipulations and have a completely reproducible pipeline. Björn has provided the source code (Stata) so it should be easy enough. For now I work with his data, work1.dta.

\subsubsection*{Import data}
\label{sec:import-data}

Import Björns dataset.

<<setup.outer, echo=FALSE, tidy=FALSE, message=FALSE>>=
library(knitr)
opts_chunk$set(results='hide', cache=TRUE, echo=FALSE, warning=FALSE, fig.pos = 'htb', tidy.opts=list(blank=FALSE, width.cutoff=50), background='white', tidy=TRUE, error=TRUE, message=FALSE, dev="pdf", autodep = TRUE)
opts_knit$set(root.dir = ".")
options(scipen=999) ## Avoid scientific formating of large numbers.
@

<<paper-iii-part-2-import.data>>=
library(readstata13)
my.dt <- setDT(readstata13::read.dta13("~/Downloads/work1.dta"))
@

\subsubsection*{Run model 1}
\label{sec:run-model-1}

The dependent variable is \texttt{deforest\_forward}, which capture how much deforestation there will be in the future five years from time $t$, which is the time when the value of the independent variables was measured. \texttt{deforest\_forward} is negative when the \texttt{forest\_coverage} is increasing.


<<paper-iii-part-2-run.model>>=
library(lme4)
library(lattice); library(latticeExtra)
library(effects)
my.dt$iwi <- scale(my.dt$iwi)
iwi_range <- range(my.dt$iwi, na.rm = TRUE)
my.dt.2 <- my.dt[anyforest > 0, ]
## my.fit.1 <- lmer(n_deforest_forward ~ iwi + I(iwi^2) + I(iwi^3) + (1 + year) + (1 | country) + (1 | toplevelregion) + (1 | areaname), data = my.dt.2)
my.fit.1 <- lmer(n_deforest_forward ~ iwi + I(iwi^2) + I(iwi^3) + I(iwi^4) + (1 + year) + (1 + country) + (1 | toplevelregion) + (1 | areaname), data = my.dt.2)
my.eff <- Effect("iwi", my.fit.1,
                 xlevels = list(iwi = seq(iwi_range[1], iwi_range[2], length.out = 100)))
## plot(my.eff, grid = TRUE)
## plot(my.eff, grid = TRUE,
##      panel = function(x, y, ...) {
##        lattice::panel.abline(h = 0, col = "red", lty = 2)
##        effects::panel.effect(x, y, ...)
##      })

## plot(my.eff, grid = TRUE, 
##      ref = list(h = 0, col = "red", lty = 2))

p <- plot(my.eff, grid = TRUE)

original_panel <- p$panel

p$panel <- function(...) {
  original_panel(...)
  lattice::panel.abline(h = 0, col = "red", lty = 2, lwd = 1.5)
}

print(p)

@ 

